  "conclusions": [
    "The special suffixes .create--- and .template-- are not disabling suffixes in the pinned fixed-C loaders.",
    "Default gmsv setup uses npcdir=data/npc, so the raw data neweq.create--- is scanned but its two blocks are commented and therefore do not instantiate NPCs.",
    "The hydata neweq.create--- contains two active NPC blocks, but hydata is not the default npcdir in the pinned setup; treating it as active requires an explicit alternate runtime configuration.",
    "hecheng/process.template-- is an exact blob duplicate of the formal eden3/process/process.template and is loader-accepted; it should be classified as duplicate residue, not promoted as a second canonical template.",
    "NPC_Util_CheckAssignArgFile extracts the file: path literally, and NPC_Util_GetArgStr opens getNpcdir()/filename; therefore file:hecheng/baoshi.arg does not fall through to baoshi.arg--.",
    "The two .arg-- files are currently source-history residues with dangling formal references. Their payloads are valid-looking StoneAge event/ITEMCHANGE DSL, but renaming or promoting them would require explicit provenance evidence."
  ],
  "policy": {
